    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.comment\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI am aware that mini.comment is intentionally designed with linewise comments in mind and avoids dealing with inline block comments. However, it is very often that I'm working with some code and have a comment at the _end_ of a line that I want to use the mini.comment textobject on. I feel like this is within the scope of mini.comment, as they can be simply limited to the single line (you'd likely not have multiline linewise comments all at the end of code?)\r\nHere's a video of what I'm talking about if it helps (I'm attempting `dgc`):\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8d546d63-5cc2-4dcd-843d-676b05f731ca\r\n\r\nThanks for your work on these amazing plugins :)\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9.5\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. use defaults of mini.comment\r\n2. try `dgc` on a regular multi-line or full single-line comment\r\n3. try `dgc` on a comment that's at the very end of a line of code/text\r\n4. observe that only the first succeeds\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nthe comment textobject (`gc` by default) should, at least by my first impression, cover both typical linewise comments and comments at the end of code / text.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nthe comment textobject only seems to work specifically for linewise comments that do NOT have code/text before them.",
