            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nHaving 'mini.comment' work on the \"end of line\" comments is indeed out of scope for 'mini.comment' because those comments are not linewise. Only \"whole line\" comments are in scope, mostly for reducing complexity. Otherwise detecting proper \"end of line\" comments is a significant challenge. For example, the comment leader can be inside a string or \"end of line\" comment itself, like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal a = '-- not a comment'\r\nlocal b = \"-- not a comment\"\r\nlocal c = [[-- not a comment]]\r\nlocal d = 1 -- comment within -- comment\r\n```\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, I can also not reproduce the deletion of next line which follows the \"end of line\" comment which I can see from the screencast. Is it something that is indeed happening? If so, could you try reproducing it with only 'mini.comment' and possibly some other options that affect it?",
