        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Hi, thanks for the quick response!\r\n\r\nI see your point with the difficulty of implementing end-of-line comments, that makes sense.\r\n\r\n> I can also not reproduce the deletion of next line which follows the \"end of line\" comment\r\n\r\nI think what you're seeing is just the window scrolling horizontally when I move to the end of the line due to the small window size, not anything being deleted. Sorry for the confusion :P\r\n\r\nI'm curious if you have any suggestions for how I _could_ accomplish this? I really love having access to the `gc` textobject but it just feels incomplete to not work on end-of-line comments. I tried adding a mini.ai treesitter textobject for `@comment.outer`, but that seems to work differently with multiple consecutive linewise comments (it only operates on the cursor's _current_ line, im guessing due to how the tree represents comments) and requires keybinds with a/i followed by a character instead of just gc. Or maybe I just deal with it instead, haha.\r\n\r\nAlso, slightly unrelated, is there anywhere I can see a comparison between nvim 0.10's built-in commenting vs mini.comment? I'm unsure based on the readme/help file if I'll need to keep this plugin around after I update.\r\n\r\nAnyways, since this seems to be outside the scope of mini.comment, feel free to close this issue any time, and thanks for your help!",
