            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I'm curious if you have any suggestions for how I _could_ accomplish this?\r\n\r\nOther than writing own textobject (almost) from scratch, I don't know about the way to achieve that relatively pain free.\r\n\r\n> Also, slightly unrelated, is there anywhere I can see a comparison between nvim 0.10's built-in commenting vs mini.comment? I'm unsure based on the readme/help file if I'll need to keep this plugin around after I update.\r\n\r\nBuilt-in commenting in Neovim>=0.10 is a toned down version of 'mini.comment', quite literally. The rule of thumb is if you use `require('mini.comment').setup()` (i.e. no configuration), then using built-in commenting might be just fine, because they are 99% the same. If you want/need extra configuration from 'mini.comment' (like custom commentstring, hooks, etc.), then 'mini.comment' is the way to go.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nClosing this as the current way 'mini.comment' works (only for per line commenting) is intended and won't change.",
